.PP
\f[B](as\-> expr name .
sexps)\f[R]
.PP
Bind \f[CR]name\f[R] to \f[CR]expr\f[R], evaluate the first
\f[CR]sexp\f[R] in the lexical context of that binding, then bind
\f[CR]name\f[R] to that result, repeating for each successive
\f[CR]sexp\f[R] in \f[CR]sexps\f[R], returning the result of the last
\f[CR]sexp\f[R].
.PP
\f[B](cond\-> expr .
clauses)\f[R]
.PP
Given an \f[CR]expr\f[R]ession and a set of
\f[CR]test\f[R]/\f[CR]sexp\f[R] pairs, thread \f[CR]x\f[R] (via
\f[B]\->\f[R]) through each \f[CR]sexp\f[R] for which the corresponding
\f[CR]test\f[R] expression is truthy, i.e.\ neither \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R]
nor \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R].
Note that, unlike \f[B]cond\f[R] branching, \f[B]cond\->\f[R] threading
does not short circuit after the first truthy test expression.
.PP
\f[B](cond\->> expr .
clauses)\f[R]
.PP
Given an \f[CR]expr\f[R]ession and a set of
\f[CR]test\f[R]/\f[CR]sexp\f[R] pairs, thread \f[CR]x\f[R] (via
\f[B]\->>\f[R]) through each \f[CR]sexp\f[R] for which the corresponding
\f[CR]test\f[R] expression is truthy, i.e.\ neither \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R]
nor \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R].
Note that, unlike \f[B]cond\f[R] branching, \f[B]cond\->>\f[R] threading
does not short circuit after the first truthy \f[CR]test\f[R]
expression.
.PP
\f[B](some\-> x .
sexps)\f[R]
.PP
When \f[CR]x\f[R] is not \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], thread it into the
first \f[CR]sexp\f[R] (via \f[B]\->\f[R]), and when that result is not
\f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], through the next, etc.
.PP
\f[B](some\->> x .
sexps)\f[R]
.PP
When \f[CR]x\f[R] is not \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], thread it into the
first \f[CR]sexp\f[R] (via \f[B]\->>\f[R]), and when that result is not
\f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], through the next, etc.
.SS Conditional Macros
\f[B](if\-let ((patt test)) then {{else}})\f[R]
.PP
If \f[CR]test\f[R] evaluates to anything other than \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R]
or \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], evaluate \f[CR]then\f[R] with
\f[CR]patt\f[R] bound to the value of \f[CR]test\f[R], otherwise
\f[CR]else\f[R], if supplied, else \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R].
.PP
\f[B](iff\-let ((patt test)) .
body)\f[R]
.PP
When \f[CR]test\f[R] evaluates to anything other than
\f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R] or \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], evaluate
\f[CR]body\f[R] with \f[CR]patt\f[R] bound to the value of
\f[CR]test\f[R], otherwise return \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R].
.PP
\f[B](condp pred expr .
clauses)\f[R]
.PP
Given a binary predicate, an expression and a set of clauses of the
form:
.IP
.EX
test\-expr result\-expr

test\-expr >> result\-fn
.EE
.PP
where \f[CR]result\-fn\f[R] is a unary function, if
\f[CR](pred test\-expr expr)\f[R] returns anything other than
\f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R] or \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R], the clause is a match.
.PP
If a binary clause matches, return \f[CR]result\-expr\f[R].
If a ternary clause matches, call \f[CR]result\-fn\f[R] with the result
of the predicate and return the result.
.PP
If no clause matches and a single default expression is given after the
clauses, return it.
If no default expression is given and no clause matches, throw a
\f[CR]no\-matching\-clause\f[R] error.
.PP
\f[B](if\-not test then)\f[R]
.PP
\f[B](if\-not test then else)\f[R]
.PP
If \f[CR]test\f[R] evaluates to \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], evaluate and return \f[CR]then\f[R], otherwise
\f[CR]else\f[R], if supplied, else \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R].
.PP
\f[B](iff test .
body)\f[R]
.PP
Like Clojure\(cqs \f[CR]when\f[R].
If \f[CR]test\f[R] evaluates to anything other than \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R]
or \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], evaluate \f[CR]body\f[R] in an implicit
\f[CR]progn\f[R].
.PP
\f[B](when\-not test .
body)\f[R]
.PP
If \f[CR]test\f[R] evaluates to \f[CR]\(aqfalse\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R], evaluate \f[CR]body\f[R] in an implicit
\f[CR]progn\f[R].
Otherwise return \f[CR]\(aqundefined\f[R].
