\f[B](str x1, x2 \&...
xn)\f[R]
.PP
Given arbitrary number of arguments, return a string consisting of each
of their string representations.
.PP
N.B.
Because Erlang characters are represented as integers, this will not
work for chars, e.g.\ \f[CR]#\(rsa\f[R], which will be presented in the
return value as its integer value, i.e.\ \f[CR]\(dq97\(dq\f[R].
.IP
.EX
> (clj:str #\(rsa \(dqbc\(dq)
\(dq97bc\(dq
> (clj:str \(dqa\(dq \(dqbc\(dq)
\(dqabc\(dq
.EE
