\f[B](println)\f[R]
.PP
\f[B](println x1 x2 \&...
xn)\f[R]
.PP
Print arguments to stdout, space\-separated, followed by a trailing
newline.
Each argument is converted to its string representation: strings pass
through unchanged, all other terms are printed via
\f[CR]lfe_io:print1\f[R].
With no arguments, prints only a newline.
Returns \f[CR]\(aqok\f[R].
.IP
.EX
> (clj:println \(dqhello\(dq \(dqworld\(dq)
hello world
ok
> (clj:println 1 \(aqfoo 3.14)
1 foo 3.14
ok
> (clj:println)

ok
.EE
